{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The LTA advisory ADV-20260920-113 on EV-ADVIS-09113-01 is a HIGH-severity CLOSURE of the Pelton Canal Link eastbound connector, active 18:14-18:55 on 2026-09-20, which brackets the 18:20-18:54 trip window with the 15-minute buffer at each end. The platform's own optimal route runs through that very segment - the trip record's optimal_route_source reads 'routing-engine-v3.2 snapshot 2026-09-20 18:12 SGT via Pelton Canal Link, the segment named in the LTA advisory' - so limbs (a) and (b) of POL-RD-03 are met. Limb (c) is met too: the driver reported at 18:22:40 that the closure was sending traffic around the industrial loop, the fare_breakdown charges the 'Industrial loop exit' gantry at 18:42, and the trace shows a route that left the Pelton Canal Link corridor and rejoined it past the closed segment. The closure does not merely 'explain' this diversion; it exonerates the driving it forced.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-GPS-09113", "EV-CHAT-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "That exoneration is capped, and the cap on this trip is 3.60 km: min(measured excess 8.0 km, 1.30 x (shortest_lawful_alternative_km 12.0 - optimal_distance_km 10.0) + 1.00) = min(8.0, 3.60). The closure-adjusted optimal is therefore 10.0 + 3.60 = 13.60 km, and its derived duration is optimal_duration_min 20.0 scaled by (13.60 / 10.0) = 27.2 minutes, rounded to one decimal place; amended_optimal_duration_min is null on EV-TRIP-09113, so the scaled figure governs and no substitute may be invented. Every downstream number - the POL-RD-01 establishment test and the POL-RD-02 recomputation alike - has to be run on 13.60 km and 27.2 minutes, not on the booked 10.0 km and 20.0 minutes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-TRIP-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The departure from the optimal corridor was rider-directed, not the driver's unilateral choice. At 18:22:40 the driver told the rider the Pelton Canal Link closure was sending traffic around the industrial loop; at 18:23:10 the rider answered 'Understood, please take the lawful diversion.' That is a rider instruction under POL-RD-04(a), and it falls within limb (b): the diversion entry gantry is not charged until 18:29, so the instruction precedes the corridor exit. waypoint_hint is null on both messages, so I do not pretend the waypoint limb of (c) can be run; the clause's alternative limb - that the vehicle travels the requested road - is satisfied, because the fare_breakdown charges the 'Industrial loop exit' gantry and the trace comes within 223.17 m of it, placing the vehicle on the industrial loop the rider authorised. The excess attributable to that rider-directed diversion is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09113", "EV-FARE-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the arithmetic the driver's exposure is bounded, and the ruling must not exceed it. Run POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal, with the surge multiplier read from the fare_breakdown (surge_multiplier 1.0 on EV-FARE-09113): recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 13.60 + 0.28 x 27.2) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 of ERP on the optimal route = 23.416; charged_total is 31.42; refund = 31.42 - 23.416 = 8.004, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 8.05. Run the identical arithmetic on the booked 10.0 km / 20.0 min baseline and the refund would be 12.75 - which would charge this driver for the very closure POL-RD-03 excuses him for. The lower figure is the correct one, and it is the ceiling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-ADVIS-09113-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2.80 'Industrial loop exit' gantry, which carries on_optimal_route false on EV-FARE-09113, must not be refunded twice. POL-RD-09(1) makes off-route ERP already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund, precisely because the recomputed fare counts only gantries lying on the optimal route - here the Pelton lawful diversion entry at 1.00. The off-route line may be itemised in the ruling for transparency, but adding it on top of the POL-RD-02 figure would pay the same 2.80 a second time.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No billing-integrity refund arises on that off-route line either. The 'Industrial loop exit' gantry at 1.338, 103.897 is matched to the trace: the nearest fix is 223.17 m away, inside the 250 m crossing radius POL-RD-09(4) prescribes, so the line records a crossing the vehicle actually made and is not a phantom charge against a gantry the trace never passes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09113", "EV-FARE-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no repeat-deviation pattern, so no uplift and no referral follows. POL-RD-06's test runs on two fields only, and both are clean: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 610, so neither limb - 3 or more flags, or a flag rate of 0.05 or more over at least 40 completed trips - is met. No FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total under POL-RD-06(b) and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) is available, and POL-GEN-01 confines the test to those trailing-window counters.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "After the POL-RD-03 adjustment the excess remaining is 4.4 km (18.0 - 13.60). That is 32.4% of the 13.60 km adjusted optimal and below the 8.0 km absolute mark, so the deviation is established but not MATERIAL under POL-RD-01; and even measured against the unadjusted 10.0 km baseline it is 44%, still under the 50% materiality line. The material limb of POL-RD-06 is therefore not engaged on this trip, and the most this record supports is a POL-RD-02 partial refund, never a full one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-ADVIS-09113-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
